  "title": "The violated line can be pinned: frozen states block the Tseitin-style width proof",
  "subject": "Whether the violated line of the knot's plane spaces can always be moved locally, as a Tseitin charge can",
  "conclusion": "In the octahedral knot spaces the violated line is a vortex of a height function, and frozen states pin it: no change within distance 3 moves it to a given adjacent line, in the bulk and in whole-sphere states of K_8, though random states always move. So the Tseitin-style resolution width proof cannot be applied state by state, and width Omega(sqrt n) reduces to a pursuit lemma for flat label states.",
